# Review

## Summary

No detail outgrows its argumentative role. The note has three short paragraphs: the claim, one worked example and the test the example implies.

The citation example in the second paragraph is the only substantial detail. It does necessary work. It shows a case where the lesson applies even though the earlier incident's surface features (the specific citations) are absent. It also shows why lookup by source name would fail while recognition of the shared feature would succeed. Without it, the abstract claim that the reviewer must "identify when they apply" would be hard to apply. The example runs about five sentences, and each one carries a step: the incident, the changed surface, the condition under which the lesson still applies, the failure of name lookup and the success of the unchanged instruction. None of them elaborates past that job.

The closing paragraph is a two-sentence test and conclusion, not added detail. Compressing any part further would leave the claim abstract.
